<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Id6da981f4bbbd276e7bc694cb1d77845a9854381" commit="fecf3090f704e6508824f7fba960ab807fc560d3" commit_message="CHROMIUM: cpu_cooling: log when cpu is thermal throttled  BUG=None TEST=Boot kernel on oak and make sure logs show up when cpus      are thermal throttled.  Change-Id: Id6da981f4bbbd276e7bc694cb1d77845a9854381 Signed-off-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335526 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="335526" owner_email="jcliang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/26/335526/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I6d06ad27038fac76e7b32c86026df8cffc1bbdf0" commit="17eedd2922ca000c1dc53972f06447af9989d61e" commit_message="CHROMIUM: arm64: dts: mt8173: Fix cpu_thermal cooling-maps contributions  According to [0], the contribution field for each cooling-device express their relative power efficiency. Higher weights express higher power efficiency.  Weighting is relative such that if each cooling device has a weight of 1 they are considered equal. This is particularly useful in heterogeneous systems where two cooling devices may perform the same kind of compute, but with different efficiency.  [0] Documentation/thermal/power_allocator.txt  According to Mediatek IC designer, the power efficiency ratio between the LITTLE core cluster (cooling-device cpu0) and big core cluster (cooling-device cpu1) is around 3:1 (3072:1024).  Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:51749 TEST=On oak-rev5, start webgl Aquarium @ 4000 fish  watch grep . /sys/class/thermal/cooling_device*/cur_state \               /sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone0/temp   =&gt; cooling_device1/cur_state starts to increase before cooling_device0.  Change-Id: I6d06ad27038fac76e7b32c86026df8cffc1bbdf0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335653 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Javi Merino &lt;javi.merino@arm.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="335653" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/53/335653/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I63718a4e94e47ca05770c564508f5a9ba99ad0a7" commit="76651ed0b48d5b7b130bb50ec4327310c9cc1a3f" commit_message="CHROMIUM: arm64: dts: mt8173-oak: Increase sustainable-power to 5 W  The sustainable-power describes how much power a thermal zone can dissipate at the desired control temperature.  For the cpu_thermal zone, the control temperature is (85).  In the binding doc [0], it actually gives some examples:    For reference, the sustainable power of a 4'' phone is typically 2000mW,  while on a 10'' tablet is around 4500mW.  Since oak is &gt;10&quot; tablet, we choose 5000 mW.  [0] Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thermal/thermal.txt  Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:51749 TEST=On oak-rev5, start webgl Aquarium @ 4000 fish  watch grep . /sys/class/thermal/cooling_device*/cur_state \               /sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone0/temp   =&gt; temperature climbs up to and hovers at ~85 C   =&gt; All 3 cooling_device*/cur_state stay almost continuously at 0  Change-Id: I63718a4e94e47ca05770c564508f5a9ba99ad0a7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335427 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="335427" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/27/335427/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Icef34578ad2260f4b56ca1f9957a35daea4ce97a" commit="1e4a1e17f127208fd8d7285dc54c9ae651e2bb86" commit_message="platform_HWwatchdog: Separate watchdog control into helper class  This patch moves most of the logic from platform_HWwatchdog into a separate helper class so the code can be reused by other tests that need to interact with the hardware watchdog.  BUG=None TEST=Ran platform_HWwatchdog on Oak.  Change-Id: Icef34578ad2260f4b56ca1f9957a35daea4ce97a Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334743 Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="334743" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/43/334743/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie00e471b5cad5048ca76a1bf13b5f4d4b9946696" commit="95d3fbeb8491b6952c2643e67e1fe42419a078bd" commit_message="firmware_EventLog: Test for hardware watchdog event  This patch adds a check for the watchdog timeout event to the firmware_EventLog test. Skipping x86 devices for now which don't seem to report this event (at least on my old Falco).  Also change all the TestError in this test to TestFail which is actually the correct exception to throw for cases where the board doesn't meet expectations (as opposed to cases where the test logic itself ran into an unexpected condition somehow).  BUG=None TEST=Ran on Oak.  Change-Id: Ie00e471b5cad5048ca76a1bf13b5f4d4b9946696 Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334744 Reviewed-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="334744" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/44/334744/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I202de94bb5b99dab6db7872bb7666fd73c18dbfa" commit="586e9bbd33e65d80818847ba2861d0ed4e502147" commit_message="graphics_GLMark2/Bench: explicitly raise TestFail.  Currently utils.run notices a negative return code and throws a CmdError. This is unhandled by the test. Somehow the harness colors the tests orange on wmatrix but the cq considers this passing. Convert the ERROR to FAIL.  TEST=Veyron output changes from END ERROR -&gt; END FAIL 20:24:16 INFO | autoserv| END ERROR graphics_GLMark2  graphics_GLMark2  timestamp=1459301055  localtime=Mar 29 20:24:15 20:24:52 INFO | autoserv| END GOOD  ----  ----  timestamp=1459301090  localtime=Mar 29 20:24:50 to 20:35:31 INFO | autoserv| END FAIL  graphics_GLMark2  graphics_GLMark2  timestamp=1459301730  localtime=Mar 29 20:35:30 20:36:08 INFO | autoserv| END GOOD  ----  ----  timestamp=1459301766  localtime=Mar 29 20:36:06 BUG=chrome-os-partner:51809  Change-Id: I202de94bb5b99dab6db7872bb7666fd73c18dbfa Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/336060 Commit-Ready: Ilja Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ilja Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="336060" owner_email="ihf@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/60/336060/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I17d8c82fd9c08082e8a070fcc839c333e79d11a6" commit="e5f28feb74288b542b4093562375aff9693517f2" commit_message="CHROMIUM: iwlwifi: mvm: add a scan timeout for regular scans  If something goes wrong with the firmware and we never get a scan complete notification, we stay stuck forever.  In order to avoid this situation, add a timeout and trigger an NMI if it expires before receiving the notification., so we can clean things up.  BUG=cheomeos-partner:48182, 50672, 49779, 50653 TEST=Keep rebooting the machine for about 6 hours and make sure that it can always connect  Change-Id: I17d8c82fd9c08082e8a070fcc839c333e79d11a6 Signed-off-by: Luca Coelho &lt;luciano.coelho@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334633 Tested-by: Matt Chen &lt;matt.chen@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Sameer Nanda &lt;snanda@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Matt Chen &lt;matt.chen@intel.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="334633" owner_email="luciano.coelho@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/33/334633/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.10" change_id="I17d8c82fd9c08082e8a070fcc839c333e79d11a6" commit="7e69cae57f9b37fd0817665655951eacc16ded4e" commit_message="CHROMIUM: iwlwifi: mvm: add a scan timeout for regular scans  If something goes wrong with the firmware and we never get a scan complete notification, we stay stuck forever.  In order to avoid this situation, add a timeout and trigger an NMI if it expires before receiving the notification., so we can clean things up.  BUG=cheomeos-partner:48182, 50672, 49779, 50653 TEST=Keep rebooting the machine for about 6 hours and make sure that it can always connect  Change-Id: I17d8c82fd9c08082e8a070fcc839c333e79d11a6 Signed-off-by: Luca Coelho &lt;luciano.coelho@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334673 Tested-by: Matt Chen &lt;matt.chen@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Sameer Nanda &lt;snanda@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Matt Chen &lt;matt.chen@intel.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="334673" owner_email="luciano.coelho@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/73/334673/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I17d8c82fd9c08082e8a070fcc839c333e79d11a6" commit="a8b40b375c03abce23d27a32ccb7e639bf77240d" commit_message="CHROMIUM: iwlwifi: mvm: add a scan timeout for regular scans  If something goes wrong with the firmware and we never get a scan complete notification, we stay stuck forever.  In order to avoid this situation, add a timeout and trigger an NMI if it expires before receiving the notification., so we can clean things up.  BUG=cheomeos-partner:48182, 50672, 49779, 50653 TEST=Keep rebooting the machine for about 6 hours and make sure that it can always connect  Change-Id: I17d8c82fd9c08082e8a070fcc839c333e79d11a6 Signed-off-by: Luca Coelho &lt;luciano.coelho@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/333755 Tested-by: Matt Chen &lt;matt.chen@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Sameer Nanda &lt;snanda@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Matt Chen &lt;matt.chen@intel.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="333755" owner_email="luciano.coelho@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/55/333755/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib8309aa4a361e77156f225e734b6081589f82b2e" commit="6d4fa2482fac6daf2699dad1de59216651a765ee" commit_message="UCM config: glados and chell: Don't apply speaker EQ/DRC to headphones  Set the OutputDspName to empty for the Headphone jack, so that get_active_dsp_name doesn't return the default &quot;speaker_eq&quot; dsp for the headphone node.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:51560 TEST=On Chell set some extreme speaker EQ values in dsp.ini, listen to headphone playback and confirm the speaker EQ/DRC is not applied.  Change-Id: Ib8309aa4a361e77156f225e734b6081589f82b2e Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/336031 Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="336031" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/31/336031/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1d44d93d328d9a6f4e1fd548b500a8ad5e1149a3" commit="88c292b917986083b7bee0f4c773da027faa276f" commit_message="Banon: Add to Strago based mainboard list for mosys  Add Banon mainboard to Strago board list for mosys.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=run &quot;emerge-banon mosys&quot;  Change-Id: I1d44d93d328d9a6f4e1fd548b500a8ad5e1149a3 Signed-off-by: David Wu &lt;David_Wu@quantatw.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335528 Commit-Ready: David Wu &lt;david_wu@quantatw.com&gt; Tested-by: David Wu &lt;david_wu@quantatw.com&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: T.H. Lin &lt;T.H_Lin@quantatw.com&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="335528" owner_email="david_wu@quantatw.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/mosys" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/mosys" ref="refs/changes/28/335528/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I825d123daec66a1edfaf56a6d588578693773db2" commit="7218f5aa4d93a294f46df8c9e0158e238f38a84b" commit_message="oak: Add support for elm  elm uses a TCPC chip (no real PD), so we need to special-case it, using logic inspired from pinky.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:51770 TEST=emerge-elm mosys; cros deploy IP mosys; mosys works  Change-Id: I825d123daec66a1edfaf56a6d588578693773db2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335523 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="335523" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/mosys" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/mosys" ref="refs/changes/23/335523/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I15bc85e3d23c424351fe61cbc6b5639f83355aeb" commit="819f4763489eb092853fc686232e19b6ea9b4b8e" commit_message="Save histograms on Chameleond and add an API to get histograms  After starting video capturing, the monitoring child process should save the histograms to the share memory, before these frames get overwritten.  It also exposes a new API for the client to get the histograms.  BUG=chromium:598387 TEST=Call the new API to get historgrams.  Change-Id: I15bc85e3d23c424351fe61cbc6b5639f83355aeb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335335 Commit-Ready: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="335335" owner_email="waihong@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/chameleon" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/chameleon" ref="refs/changes/35/335335/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8a5dd1e06197329096dcd8d9d3326a4e7ea839e8" commit="b06aa91985bbf04834532429c55a0a1f7d805a1e" commit_message="logging_GenerateCrashFiles: Add SSH timeout to crash command  logging_GenerateCrashFiles.KERNEL currently takes forever (or, more precisely, 15 minutes) to complete, because the crashing SSH command never completes from the server's point of view and it waits the whole -o ServerAliveInterval=900 seconds (as hardcoded in ssh_host.py) until it tries to continue the test. Let's add an explicit (but ignored) timeout to make this less tedious to run.  BUG=None TEST=Ran on Oak.  Change-Id: I8a5dd1e06197329096dcd8d9d3326a4e7ea839e8 Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335572 Reviewed-by: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="335572" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/72/335572/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><lkgm version="8128.0.0-rc2"/></manifest>